   "id": 668992,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stem_html": "<ol class=\"os-raise-noindent\" start=\"4\">\n    <li>Suppose it costs $3 per hour to park, with a maximum cost of $12. Here is a graph of the situation.</li>\n</ol><br><img alt=\"\" class=\"img-fluid atto_image_button_text-bottom\" height=\"298\" src=\"exercises/media/d6cf9b8be3897f68.jpg\" width=\"300\"><br><br>    <p>What does the point <span data-math=\"(2,6)\">(2,6)</span> mean in this situation?</p>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1333661,
     "content_html": "6 hours of parking costs a total of $2"
    },
    {
     "id": 1333662,
     "content_html": "2 hours of parking costs a total of $6"
    },
    {
     "id": 1333663,
     "content_html": "6 hours of parking costs $2 per hour"
    },
